I am relatively new to Nethack (a macintosh version of hack) and find it
rather compelling. The game seems to have accumulated a considerable
'culture' during its long evolution. However, one problem brings me
continual grief: that of feeding characters.

Avoiding traps, killing (or avoiding) monsters, collecting and using
treasure/magic items seems easy by comparison to feeding one's character. As
I understand it there are several potential sources of sustainance:

a) Initial food rations.

b) Comestibles found in the dungeon or on killed monsters.

c) Divine intervention (i.e. praying)

d) Magic items.

e) Monster corpses.


These have drawbacks. (a) runs out quickly and for some classes of character
does not exist anyway. (b) and (e) can be poisonous with rapid and
unfortunate effects; the toxicity of (e) is *not* related to monster type.
(c) does work on a regualar basis! (d) is *very* hard to find.

85% of my charcaters die due to starvation, either directly or because they
faint from hunger in the middle of a serious combat. What am I missing? Is
there another way to eat - a cafe perhaps?? The shopkeeper always sells
dodgy rations, so he is not an option.

Answers much appreciated.

Cheers,
Jan.

